  "id": "Compound::DB01194 - Gene::759",
  "verbalization": "Brinzolamide appears to interact with Ca1 through a shared pathway involving the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide. The evidence suggests that Brinzolamide binds to Ca5a, Ca7, or Ca9, all of which participate in the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide, which in turn is participated by Ca1. This indicates a potential mechanism where Brinzolamide may influence Ca1 through a common intermediate, the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide. The consistent involvement of these calcium ions in the same biochemical process suggests a possible functional relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The evidence supports a link between Brinzolamide and Ca1 through a shared pathway, but further investigation is needed to determine the precise mechanism of action.",
